/.github/CODEOWNERS  @chamaya00
/CLAUDE.md           @chamaya00

# Everything below was added by the security review in
# `docs/security/2026-09-10-public-repo-audit.md`. Each entry is a path an
# agent run can already write to, and whose contents steer a later run or get
# executed by one - the two ways a merged diff outlives the run that wrote it.

# The engineer's Bash allowlist grants `bash tests/*`, `./tests/*`,
# `bash scripts/*` and `./scripts/*`, and it holds `Write` and `Edit` as well.
# A run that can author the script it is allowed to execute has an unscoped
# shell, whatever the allowlist says. Review is what keeps that shell from
# reaching `main`.
/tests/              @chamaya00
/scripts/            @chamaya00

# Read at the start of every run by every role, and never re-read critically -
# lessons are meant to be trusted. The project guard checks only that these
# files are inside their 40-line cap; nothing checks what the lines say. A
# single merged edit here steers every future run on this repository.
/.claude/memory/     @chamaya00

# The role prompts, the skills, and the slash commands. The project guard
# already refuses these from a non-maintainer; this makes the same rule hold
# at review time rather than only in CI.
/.claude/            @chamaya00
